      "summary": "The change otherwise addresses the stated identity, telemetry, trace, and alert requirements. Cookie header sanitization has a reachable case where a later credential remains in the output.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/TelemetryRedaction.cs",
          "line": 69,
          "message": "Cookie header sanitization leaves later cookie pairs intact. Redact the full header value so credentials after the first pair cannot pass through.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Sanitize uses SecretPattern to redact cookie headers, but the pattern consumes only the first non-whitespace token after `cookie:`.",
            "failureScenario": "Given `Cookie: first=ok; session=CANARY-TOKEN`, Sanitize replaces `first=ok;` but leaves `session=CANARY-TOKEN` in its output. A multi-cookie header can therefore expose a credential through this sanitizer. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
